# Artifacts this harness brings to every run: settings, skills, MCP config, hooks, anything its CLI
# reads. Drop the file in this folder, then add a line naming it and where it goes under the CLI's
# home ($HOME, the workspace's .home):
#
#   <file in this folder>   <where it goes under $HOME>
#
# For example, a Claude Code skill:
#
#   review.md               .claude/skills/review/SKILL.md
#
# run.sh puts each one in place before every turn. Lines starting with # are skipped, so as it
# ships, this file brings nothing.
